d assert both consumers resolve the same platform entry.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Specify how semgrep integrity is pinned given it is a multi-wheel `pip install` (e.g. pin the semgrep version plus a hash-locked requirements/`--require-hashes` set, or install a pinned self-contained artifact), distinct from gitleaks' single-tarball artifact hash, so the manifest and the Make target's hash check are implementable for both scanners.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Dockerfile.reviewbot:59-61 fetches gitleaks as one tarball (a natural artifact hash); lines 68-71 do `python -m venv /opt/semgrep && /opt/semgrep/bin/pip install --no-cache-dir semgrep` — a multi-wheel pip install, not a single downloadable artifact","Plan uniformly says 'pin Semgrep and Gitleaks versions plus artifact hashes' and AC1 says 'downloadable artifact hashes'","For pip-installed semgrep, hash integrity requires a pinned/`--require-hashes` transitive lock (or a pinned wheel + its deps), a different mechanism than a single artifact digest"],"finding":"The manifest's 'artifact hash' mechanism is well-defined for gitleaks (a single downloadable tarball) but not for semgrep, which the review-bot image installs via `pip install semgrep` into a venv, pulling many transitive wheels rather than one downloadable artifact — so a single 'downloadable artifact hash' does not model semgrep provisioning.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f2bd59e3af0f295b0","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach ('Pin Semgrep and Gitleaks versions plus artifact hashes'); Acceptance Criteria line 1","norm_id":"ne3cb0c583cb0f0f3","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Author writes one artifact-hash field per scanner in the manifest and finds semgrep has no single hash to pin, or pins only the top-level wheel while transitive deps float","The 'wrong version/hash' provisioning test for semgrep has no coherent single-hash to assert against"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Model the manifest with per-scanner provisioning modes: gitleaks = pinned version + tarball SHA256; semgrep = pinned version + a hash-locked (`--require-hashes`) requirements file covering transitive wheels. Have both the Dockerfile and the Make target consume that manifest so the 'wrong hash' failure path is defined for each.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify how semgrep integrity is pinned given it is a multi-wheel `pip install`, not a single downloadable binary (e.g. a hash-locked requirements/`--require-hashes` file or a pinned wheel set), and reconcile that with the single 'artifact hash' model that fits gitleaks.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.1,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'Pin Semgrep and Gitleaks versions plus artifact hashes.'","AC-1: 'Semgrep and Gitleaks versions and downloadable artifact hashes are single-sourced'","infra/compose/Dockerfile.reviewbot:68-70 installs semgrep via `/opt/semgrep/bin/pip install --no-cache-dir semgrep` (a PyPI package = many per-platform wheels, no single artifact hash)","infra/compose/Dockerfile.reviewbot:56-61 installs gitleaks as one GitHub release tarball (a single hashable artifact) — the two install models differ","EVIDENCE CLASS: Partially-verified — both tools exist and are installed today, but the specific 'single artifact hash' surface is only true for gitleaks"],"finding":"The plan's uniform 'downloadable artifact hashes' pinning model does not fit semgrep, which the review-bot image installs as a multi-wheel `pip install semgrep` (Dockerfile.reviewbot:68-70), not a single downloadable binary artifact like gitleaks' release tarball.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f3f73085ba5077803","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Acceptance Criteria line 1","norm_id":"n5a0b70369929e92b","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Author tries to record one semgrep hash in the manifest and finds pip resolves platform-specific wheels","The 'wrong-hash' test the plan promises has no well-defined semgrep artifact to hash"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Split the manifest's integrity model per tool: pin gitleaks by release-tarball sha256, and pin semgrep via a hash-locked requirements entry (`semgrep==X.Y.Z --hash=sha256:...` with `pip install --require-hashes`), and have both the Dockerfile and the provisioning helper consume the respective form.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Acknowledge the existing Dockerfile rationale (dynamic `latest` to avoid a pinned-version 404; unpinned Semgrep pip) and justify why single-sourced version+hash pinning supersedes it — e.g., cite Gitleaks' per-release checksums/stable asset URLs and the reproducibility/supply-chain gain that outweighs the 404 risk.","cohort":["T1"],"criteria":["T1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.1789,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["infra/compose/Dockerfile.reviewbot:47-48: 'A standalone Go binary; the latest release is resolved dynamically (arch-aware) to avoid a pinned-version 404.'","infra/compose/Dockerfile.reviewbot:68-69 installs Semgrep via unpinned `pip install --no-cache-dir semgrep`.","Plan Approach: 'Pin Semgrep and Gitleaks versions plus artifact hashes' — directly overrides the existing 'resolved dynamically ... to avoid a pinned-version 404' choice with no discussion of why pinning is now safe/preferable.","Web-confirmed prior art: Gitleaks publishes per-release SHA256 `_checksums.txt` and stable per-arch tarball URLs (github.com/gitleaks/gitleaks/releases), so a pinned URL is retrievable — but the plan should state this to close the 404 concern the current code raised."],"finding":"The plan reverses a deliberate, documented existing design decision — dynamic `latest` resolution for Gitleaks and unpinned Semgrep pip install — without acknowledging or refuting the prior rationale recorded in the current Dockerfile.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f9a1fb136cc08dd1a","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Scope (scanner version manifest and review-bot Dockerfile)","norm_id":"nf6278fbaae170563","priority":0.5211,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reviewer or maintainer sees the plan pin a version and reintroduce exactly the 404-fragility class the current dynamic resolution was written to avoid.","The manifest's pinned URL scheme diverges from Gitleaks' actual release-asset naming and reintroduces the 404 the comment warns about."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Add a short note to the Approach section stating the manifest pins to Gitleaks' published per-release asset URLs + `_checksums.txt` SHA256 (which are stable, so the 404 the current comment cites does not apply) and pins Semgrep to a specific pip version, superseding the dynamic-`latest`/unpinned choices for reproducibility.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7778,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"medium","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["3 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Document the manifest as the single source of truth and the version-bump procedure in an AGENTS.md/README/ADR note referenced by the plan.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"crit